//! **DefEq soundness of the THREE-WAY conversion algorithm** — the missing half
//! of the def-eq direction pair, and it is UNCONDITIONAL.
//!
//! Not to be confused with `wh3_soundness.rs`, which proves the three-way loop
//! sound against `par_reduces_cd_star`. This file moves that conclusion to
//! `DefEq` and carries it up to the conversion algorithm itself.
//!
//! # The gap this closes
//!
//! `def_eq_fuel_complete_wh3_final` gives COMPLETENESS at the three-way loop and
//! is premise-free. Its soundness counterpart did not exist. The only soundness
//! statement in the tree, `def_eq_fuel_wh_sound_hw` (`wh_hiota_repair.rs`), is
//! about the **two-way** loop, so the two proved halves were about two different
//! algorithms and did not compose into a sound-and-complete pair. Certificate
//! 2d records that gap. They now pair: same loop, both directions, and neither
//! side carries an undischarged residual.
//!
//! # What is proved
//!
//! * `def_eq_fuel_wh3_sound_hw` — acceptance implies `DefEq`, over a pre-pass
//!   iota residual constrained to be DefEq-sound.
//! * `hiotad3_discharged` — that residual, DISCHARGED. So
//! * `def_eq_fuel_wh3_sound` : `def_eq_fuel_wh3 the_red_env n a b = true ->
//!   DefEq a b`, for every fuel and every pair, **with no hypothesis at all**.
//! * `def_eq_fuel_wh3_accepts_sound` — the same over `DefEqFuelAcceptsWh3`, the
//!   exact object completeness produces, so the two halves compose literally
//!   rather than by analogy.
//!
//! # A claim this file used to make, and why it was wrong
//!
//! An earlier draft asserted that a premise-free version was out of reach
//! because a DefEq-flavoured `whc3_iota_sound_at` was needed and that lemma
//! "CONSUMES a `par_reduces_cd_star` major-premise hypothesis, so the par
//! discharge does not transfer by rewriting." **That was false, and it was
//! refuted by measuring rather than by argument.** `whc3_iota_sound_at` touches
//! `par_reduces_cd*` at exactly nine sites. Eight are the same rewrite this
//! file already uses. The ninth is the iota step itself, and it transfers
//! because `iota_reduces.mk` and `par_reduces_cd.iota` take **the same**
//! `iota_step (red_rec the_red_env) e e'` proof — so
//! `par_subsumes_par_cd_star … (par_reduces_cd.iota … X)` becomes
//! `DefEq.iota e2 r (iota_reduces.mk e2 r X)`, with no star wrapper because
//! `DefEq` is already the full equivalence. Zero `par_` references survive in
//! either transformed term.
//!
//! # Provenance of the proof terms
//!
//! Three of the four `*_defeq_hw` terms are the corresponding `*_wh3_par_hw`
//! proof from `wh3_hiota_repair.rs` with the conclusion relation moved from
//! `par_reduces_cd_star the_red_env` to `DefEq`. The fourth,
//! `def_eq_fuel_wh3_sound_hw`, has a different provenance and saying otherwise
//! would be wrong: `wh3_hiota_repair.rs` declares no `def_eq_fuel_wh3_*_par_hw`,
//! so that one is a `wh` -> `wh3` rename of the accepted TWO-WAY
//! `def_eq_fuel_wh_sound_hw`, valid because `def_eq_fuel_wh3_succ` has the same
//! shape as `def_eq_fuel_wh_succ`.
//!
//! The rewrite is not invented here — `wh_hiota_repair.rs` carries BOTH a par
//! and a DefEq family for the two-way loop, already kernel-accepted, and that
//! pair defines the table: `par_reduces_cd_star_app` -> `DefEq.app_cong`,
//! `..._proj` -> `DefEq.proj_cong`, `..._trans` -> `DefEq.trans`,
//! `..._spine` -> `defeq_spine`, `....refl` -> `DefEq.refl`, and the three
//! reduction-justification blocks to `DefEq.beta` / `defeq_of_zeta_step` /
//! `defeq_of_const_delta`. The three-way `WhStepR` scaffolding is untouched.
//!
//! # Stage placement
//!
//! This stage must run AFTER `add_hiotap3_discharge`: `whcd3_iota_sound_at`
//! consumes six helpers minted there (`whc_fires_plain_gen`,
//! `kapp_args_kapp_fn_nil`, `kapp_fn_kapp_fn`, `list_split_at_head`,
//! `list_take_append_gen`, `list_take_len_of_head`). The only consumer of what
//! this stage produces is `add_wh3_defeq_pair` below, which is later still, so
//! sitting late is free.
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

use crate::spec::error::SpecError;
use crate::spec::Specification;

impl Specification {
    /// The three-way DefEq soundness chain, and its discharge.
    pub(super) fn add_wh3_defeq_soundness(&mut self) -> Result<(), SpecError> {
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_DEFEQ_SPINE,
            "defeq_spine: DefEq is a congruence along an application spine. The par twin is par_reduces_cd_star_spine; this drops its RedEnv binder because DefEq is pinned at the_red_env, and closes each cons with DefEq.app_cong plus DefEq.refl on the argument. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_WHCD3_IOTA_SOUND_AT,
            "whcd3_iota_sound_at: the three-way iota residual fires only at a genuine DefEq. The par twin whc3_iota_sound_at touches par at nine sites; eight are the standard rewrite and the ninth is the iota step, which transfers because iota_reduces.mk and par_reduces_cd.iota consume the SAME iota_step proof. This is what makes the discharge below possible. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_HIOTAD3_DISCHARGED,
            "hiotad3_discharged: THE IOTA RESIDUAL, DISCHARGED IN DEFEQ FORM. The blanket iota premise is FALSE — it quantifies over every pre-pass whatsoever, and one returning an unrelated constructor application fires the rule with the wrong fields. Constrained to a DefEq-sound pre-pass it is not merely satisfiable but PROVABLE, exactly as its par twin hiotap3_discharged is. This is what lets the capstone drop its hypothesis. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_REDUCE_APP_HEAD_WH3_DEFEQ_HW,
            "reduce_app_head_wh3_defeq_hw: the application-head step of the THREE-WAY algorithm is a DefEq, with the pre-pass CONSTRAINED to be DefEq-sound. Nine head shapes: the lambda head is DefEq.beta and the eight lifting shapes are DefEq.app_cong. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_REDUCE_ONCE_RED_WH3_DEFEQ_HW,
            "reduce_once_red_wh3_defeq_hw: one three-way step is a DefEq. The delta arm goes through defeq_of_const_delta and the let arm through defeq_of_zeta_step rather than building a one-step par reduction and closing it with refl; the proj arm is DefEq.proj_cong. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_WHNF_FUEL_RED_WH3_DEFEQ_HW,
            "whnf_fuel_red_wh3_defeq_hw: the whole three-way whnf loop is a DefEq, over a constrained pre-pass. At the single site where the pre-pass is chosen the required proof is the Nat.rec induction hypothesis already in scope, so the constraint costs nothing where it is used. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_DEF_EQ_FUEL_WH3_SOUND_HW,
            "def_eq_fuel_wh3_sound_hw: soundness of the three-way conversion algorithm, over a constrained pre-pass. Nat.rec on the fuel; zero contradicts through def_eq_fuel_wh3_zero, and at succ def_eq_fuel_wh3_succ exposes the two whnf results, opt_rec_bool_true_inv inverts both, and the accepted pair is chained a to na to nb to b by DefEq.trans using whnf_fuel_red_wh3_defeq_hw on each side (DefEq.symm on the right) and def_eq_struct_sound in the middle. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_DEF_EQ_FUEL_WH3_SOUND,
            "def_eq_fuel_wh3_sound: SOUNDNESS OF THE THREE-WAY CONVERSION ALGORITHM, UNCONDITIONALLY — if def_eq_fuel_wh3 accepts a against b at any fuel, then DefEq a b. No hypothesis: the pre-pass residual is discharged by hiotad3_discharged. \
\
This is the half the system did not have. def_eq_fuel_complete_wh3_final proves COMPLETENESS at this same loop and is itself premise-free; the only soundness statement in the tree, def_eq_fuel_wh_sound_hw, is about the TWO-WAY loop. Two proved halves about two different algorithms are not a sound-and-complete pair, and certificate section 2d recorded that gap. They now pair, on the same loop, with neither side carrying a residual. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_DEF_EQ_FUEL_WH3_ACCEPTS_SOUND_HW,
            "def_eq_fuel_wh3_accepts_sound_hw: acceptance implies DefEq, stated over DefEqFuelAcceptsWh3 rather than over a specific fuel, by eliminating that inductive. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_DEF_EQ_FUEL_WH3_ACCEPTS_SOUND,
            "def_eq_fuel_wh3_accepts_sound: acceptance implies DefEq, unconditionally, over the EXACT object def_eq_fuel_complete_wh3_final produces. This is what makes the pairing literal rather than an analogy between two similar-looking statements: completeness ends at DefEqFuelAcceptsWh3 a b and soundness starts there. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        Ok(())
    }
}

const SRC_DEFEQ_SPINE: &str = "def defeq_spine (xs : ListType KExpr) : forall (u : KExpr) (v : KExpr), DefEq u v -> DefEq (apply_spine xs u) (apply_spine xs v) := ListType.rec KExpr (fun (l : ListType KExpr) => forall (u : KExpr) (v : KExpr), DefEq u v -> DefEq (apply_spine l u) (apply_spine l v)) (fun (u : KExpr) (v : KExpr) (hp : DefEq u v) => hp) (fun (y : KExpr) (rest : ListType KExpr) (ih : forall (u : KExpr) (v : KExpr), DefEq u v -> DefEq (apply_spine rest u) (apply_spine rest v)) => (fun (u : KExpr) (v : KExpr) (hp : DefEq u v) => ih (KExpr.app u y) (KExpr.app v y) (DefEq.app_cong u v y y hp (DefEq.refl y)))) xs";

